   "subject": "GNU R API Exception for Stats Function",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hello -\r<br>\r<br>I am currently in the process of trying to incorporate the &#39;arima&#39; \r<br>function from the stats package.  So far, I have been able to bring in \r<br>the necessary c code and compile from source.  However, when running the \r<br>function, I receive the following run time exception :\r<br>\r<br>sys::Err: org.renjin.eval.EvalException: Exception calling list(name = \r<br>ARIMA_CSS, address = org.renjin.sexp.ExternalPtr@5879d74e, numParameters \r<br>= c(6L)) : Unimplemented GNU R API function &#39;Rf_ScalarReal&#39;\r<br>\r<br>Not sure where to go from here!\r<br>\r<br>Thanks in advance,\r<br>\r<br>-- \r<br>Philip Buonomo\r<br>Project Manager\r<br>Pacific Controls Inc.\r<br>230 Davidson Avenue, Somerset, New Jersey 08873 USA\r<br>Tel.: <a href=\"tel:(732)%20748-0060\" value=\"+17327480060\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+1 732 748 0060</a> Fax: <a href=\"tel:(732)%20748-9300\" value=\"+17327489300\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+1 732 748 9300</a>\r<br>Mobile: <a href=\"tel:(862)%20219-8680\" value=\"+18622198680\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+1 862 219 8680</a>\r<br>Email: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">buo...@pacificcontrols.net</a>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "QJ3OY1qSBgAJ",
   "from": "Bertram, Alexander",
   "author": "f06db63329fab1f9",
   "date": "2016-04-15T08:18:20Z",
   "subject": "Re: GNU R API Exception for Stats Function",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Philip,<div><br></div><div>Great that you&#39;re digging into this!</div><div><br></div><div>What I&#39;ve done is generate stubs for all the GNU R API methods into this Java package:</div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/tree/master/tools/gnur-runtime/src/main/java/org/renjin/gnur/api\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/tree/master/tools/gnur-runtime/src/main/java/org/renjin/gnur/api&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343757828000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1wcY3jJCU42tmrPVElNBKR\">https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/tree/master/tools/gnur-runtime/src/main/java/org/renjin/gnur/api</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>So that things compile at least, and then we can implement the most-used methods as needed.</div><div><br></div><div>You can find the stub for the Rf_ScalarReal function here:</div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/blob/master/tools/gnur-runtime/src/main/java/org/renjin/gnur/api/Rinternals.java#L1586-1586\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/blob/master/tools/gnur-runtime/src/main/java/org/renjin/gnur/api/Rinternals.java%23L1586-1586&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343757828000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Z4XsznAubU5tNUD600uTi\">https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/blob/master/tools/gnur-runtime/src/main/java/org/renjin/gnur/api/Rinternals.java#L1586-1586</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>There isn&#39;t a great source of documentation for the GNU R API beyond the GNU R source itself:</div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/wch/r-source/blob/e5b21d0397c607883ff25cca379687b86933d730/src/include/Rinlinedfuns.h#L599\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/wch/r-source/blob/e5b21d0397c607883ff25cca379687b86933d730/src/include/Rinlinedfuns.h%23L599&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343757828000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2WXLS8-Xyl5YAok5qQlB-D\">https://github.com/wch/r-source/blob/e5b21d0397c607883ff25cca379687b86933d730/src/include/Rinlinedfuns.h#L599</a></div><div><br></div><div>but Hadley has a partial guide in his Advanced R book:</div><div><a href=\"http://adv-r.had.co.nz/C-interface.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://adv-r.had.co.nz/C-interface.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343757828000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ssGXbkwsfSNLdvS3OTJ1J\">http://adv-r.had.co.nz/C-interface.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>The ScalarXX functions basically create vectors of length one from the given scalar arguments. </div><div><br></div><div>So you can update the stub in Rinternals.java</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:9pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">public static </span>SEXP <span style=\"background-color:rgb(228,228,255)\">Rf_ScalarReal</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">double </span>p0) {<br>  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">throw new </span>UnimplementedGnuApiMethod(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,0);font-weight:bold\">&quot;Rf_ScalarReal&quot;</span>);<br>}</pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:9pt\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;white-space:normal\">to the following:</div></pre></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:9pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">public static </span>SEXP Rf_ScalarReal(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">double </span>x) {<br>  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">return new </span>DoubleArrayVector(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:9pt\">x</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:9pt\">);</span><br><font color=\"#000000\">}<br></font></pre></div><div>And that should be enough.</div><div><br></div><div>If you can take a second to update the ScalarXXX functions as part of the pull request that would be great!</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Alex</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Apr 15, 2016 at 2:12 AM, Philip Buonomo <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">buo...@pacificcontrols.net</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
