w.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/wch/r-source/blob/e5b21d0397c607883ff25cca379687b86933d730/src/include/Rinlinedfuns.h%23L599&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343757831000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2owgfWFslDUIqzYNNjdQDK\">https://github.com/wch/r-source/blob/e5b21d0397c607883ff25cca379687b86933d730/src/include/Rinlinedfuns.h#L599</a></div><div><br></div><div>but Hadley has a partial guide in his Advanced R book:</div><div><a href=\"http://adv-r.had.co.nz/C-interface.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://adv-r.had.co.nz/C-interface.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343757831000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Zel0y2B196_f0ajzKTHPp\">http://adv-r.had.co.nz/C-interface.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>The ScalarXX functions basically create vectors of length one from the given scalar arguments. </div><div><br></div><div>So you can update the stub in Rinternals.java</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:9pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">public static </span>SEXP <span style=\"background-color:rgb(228,228,255)\">Rf_ScalarReal</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">double </span>p0) {<br>  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">throw new </span>UnimplementedGnuApiMethod(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,0);font-weight:bold\">&quot;Rf_ScalarReal&quot;</span>);<br>}</pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:9pt\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;white-space:normal\">to the following:</div></pre></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:9pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">public static </span>SEXP Rf_ScalarReal(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">double </span>x) {<br>  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font