    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Alexander -<div><br></div><div>Thanks for the guidance on this topic.  In addition to these methods, there are some additional GNU API methods which have been required.  I&#39;ve been working through these but haven&#39;t spent too much time as of yet.  </div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ll reply to this chain if there any road blocks I run into - otherwise once the function evaluates properly I&#39;ll submit a pull request.</div><div><br></div><div>Regards -</div><div><br></div><div>Philip</div><div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Saturday, April 16, 2016 at 7:42:50 PM UTC-4, Alexander Bertram wrote:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Philip,<div>I&#39;ve actually just merged a branch that had implementations of these particular functions, they are now implemented in the latest release of Renjin.</div><div><br>Best,</div><div>Alex</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Friday, April 15, 2016 at 10:18:20 AM UTC+2, Alexander Bertram wrote:</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Philip,<div><br></div><div>Great that you&#39;re digging into this!</div><div><br></div><div>What I&#39;ve done is generate stubs for all the GNU R API methods into this Java package:</div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/tree/master/tools/gnur-runtime/src/main/java/org/renjin/gnur/api\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/tree/master/tools/gnur-runtime/src/main/java/org/renjin/gnur/api&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343757835000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1pCjDZIvaShI4NCOkahh4S\">https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/tree/master/tools/gnur-runtime/src/main/java/org/renjin/gnur/api</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>So that things compile at least, and then we can implement the most-used methods as needed.</div><div><br></div><div>You can find the stub for the Rf_ScalarReal function here:</div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/blob/master/tools/gnur-runtime/src/main/java/org/renjin/gnur/api/Rinternals.java#L1586-1586\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/blob/master/tools/gnur-runtime/src/main/java/org/renjin/gnur/api/Rinternals.java%23L1586-1586&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343757835000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0CMBTPIZv8FQbUfknw4rEB\">https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/blob/master/tools/gnur-runtime/src/main/java/org/renjin/gnur/api/Rinternals.java#L1586-1586</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>There isn&#39;t a great source of documentation for the GNU R API beyond the GNU R source itself:</div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/wch/r-source/blob/e5b21d0397c607883ff25cca379687b86933d730/src/include/Rinlinedfuns.h#L599\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/wch/r-source/blob/e5b21d0397c607883ff25cca379687b86933d730/src/include/Rinlinedfuns.h%23L599&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343757835000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Re99tEK2Rwc26IhU9l9p6\">https://github.com/wch/r-source/blob/e5b21d0397c607883ff25cca379687b86933d730/src/include/Rinlinedfuns.h#L599</a></div><div><br></div><div>but Hadley has a partial guide in his Advanced R book:</div><div><a href=\"http://adv-r.had.co.nz/C-interface.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://adv-r.had.co.nz/C-interface.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343757835000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Cbq99u8GNUlLXMy3e5gKI\">http://adv-r.had.co.nz/C-interface.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>The ScalarXX functions basically create vectors of length one from the given scalar arguments. </div><div><br></div><div>So you can update the stub in Rinternals.java</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:9pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">public static </span>SEXP <span style=\"background-color:rgb(228,228,255)\">Rf_ScalarReal</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">double </span>p0) {<br>  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">throw new </span>UnimplementedGnuApiMethod(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,0);font-weight:bold\">&quot;Rf_ScalarReal&quot;</span>);<br>}</pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:9pt\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;white-space:normal\">to the following:</div></pre></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;font-size:9pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">public static </span>SEXP Rf_ScalarReal(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">double </span>x) {<br>  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,128);font-weight:bold\">return new </span>DoubleArrayVector(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:9pt\">x</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:9pt\">);</span><br><font color=\"#000000\">}<br></font></pre></div><div>And that should be enough.</div><div><br></div><div>If you can take a second to update the ScalarXXX functions as part of the pull request that would be great!</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Alex</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Apr 15, 2016 at 2:12 AM, Philip Buonomo <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">buo...@pacificcontrols.net</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Hello -<br>\r\n<br>\r\nI am currently in the process of trying to incorporate the &#39;arima&#39; function from the stats package.  So far, I have been able to bring in the necessary c code and compile from source.  However, when running the function, I receive the following run time exception :<br>\r\n<br>\r\nsys::Err: org.renjin.eval.EvalException: Exception calling list(name = ARIMA_CSS, address = org.renjin.sexp.ExternalPtr@5879d74e, numParameters = c(6L)) : Unimplemented GNU R API function &#39;Rf_ScalarReal&#39;<br>\r\n<br>\r\nNot sure where to go from here!<br>\r\n<br>\r\nThanks in advance,</blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
